#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""night-precheck: the night manager automation's precheck (spec section 8). Exit 0 = start the agent; anything
else = skip the run, which costs nothing.

  night-precheck                 what is due now, one line each:
                                   DUE <name> idle=<n>min        a coordinator to check in on
                                   DUE <name> improve idle=<n>min  improve mode is on for it and it has been idle
                                                                 IMPROVE_IDLE_MIN (30): resume its cycle
                                   DUE <name> wrapup idle=<n>min waited=<h>h  the period ended, no `lane-improve drained` yet
                                   DUE <name> wrapup idle=<n>min cap=<items|weekly>:<n>/<max>  a cap of the mode (--max-items,
                                                                 --stop-at) is reached, no `lane-improve drained` yet
                                   OFFLINE <runner,...> repo=<r> self-hosted runners not online
                                   BUDGET push-and-handover (<why>) check-ins ask only to push and hand over
                                   BUDGET unknown (<why>) ...    no budget reading: no check-ins (said once a night)
  night-precheck --checked <name> record that <name> was just checked in on (the night manager runs it after
                                   each check-in), so it is not due again for RECHECK_MIN minutes
  night-precheck --checked <name> improve|wrapup
                                   the same for an improve or wrap-up line: not due again for IMPROVE_IDLE_MIN minutes,
                                   then for as long as it stays idle (the wait doubles, at most 8 h)
  night-precheck --find <name>   where to send <name> its check-in: `<harness> <handle> <title>` on one line (title
                                   last, it may have spaces; the handle is `-` when Orca has none to give). Exit 1 and
                                   the reason on stderr when it cannot be found: send it nothing.

Due only while the owner counts as away (LANE_OWNER_AWAY from lane-limits.sh: night, NIGHT_START-NIGHT_END, or the
away file; a stopped budget never counts, since a check-in spends budget), and then for a coordinator idle at least
IDLE_MIN minutes and not checked in on for RECHECK_MIN minutes, or a runner of RUNNER_REPOS offline. Idle is the
newest write of the coordinator's own session (the one started with LANE_ROLE/LANE_PERSONA), read by its harness
adapter; Orca's terminal output is no idle signal (status-line redraws keep it fresh).

A coordinator's harness and address are not in machine.conf (`<name> <checkout>`; a third and fourth column, harness
and terminal title, override): they are looked up from Orca, as the single agent terminal whose folder is the
checkout. No agent terminal there, several, or Orca not answering is said on stderr (which project, why, Orca once) and
that coordinator is skipped: nobody is woken on a guess. Orca is asked only when a line lacks its harness or title.

Improve mode (core/improve.py; `lane-improve on`) is separate from presence: it does not make the owner count as away,
and its nudges go out by day or night whatever presence says (the plain check-ins above wait for the owner to be away).
For a coordinator it covers, the plain check-in is replaced by `DUE <name> improve`: a fallback nudge for a lost wake, since the
coordinator starts its next cycle itself. Metered, it follows that project's budget steps (budget-state --project): from
no-new-work it is the push-and-handover check-in (a BUDGET push-and-handover line first, as for a plain one), at the stop
step none, and a BUDGET unknown line when the feed gives no reading. Unmetered (improve.json) it is not gated
by budget and never reports unknown. Night alone never starts improve work. A coordinator that ran `lane-improve rest`
(nothing within the limits left) is not nudged for 12 h. After the mode ends (`lane-improve off` or its end time) each
coordinator still to wrap up gets `DUE <name> wrapup` (by day or night, none at the stop step) until it runs
`lane-improve drained`; `waited=` counts the hours since the end, so a drain nobody wrapped up shows.
A project whose cap is reached (--max-items: away-merges counted from away-merge's own record; --stop-at: weekly use from
budget-state --project) is treated like an ended period for that project alone: no improve nudge, a `wrapup ... cap=` line
instead (not at the stop step), until it runs `lane-improve drained`; a wrapped-up project gets nothing more.

Budget gate (budget-state, free), as the machine coordinator's night routine had it: at the no-new-work and
push-and-handover steps, or with the short window at WINDOW_WARN_PCT (95) or WINDOW_STOP_PCT (98), check-ins still go
out but only to have coordinators push and write their handover (a `BUDGET push-and-handover` line comes first); at
the stop step none. When the budget is unknown (no config, no usage feed, a feed that gives no reading) nobody gets a
check-in: if a coordinator would be due, one BUDGET line says so once a night (stamp
~/.cache/lane-control/night/.budget-unknown, 16 h); otherwise only stderr does, and machine-check reports the unknown
budget once. Runners are reported either way.

A project marked paused in its settings store (project-pause) is skipped; a settings file that cannot be read means
no check-in for it, said on stderr. Coordinators and runner repos come from ~/.config/lane-control/machine.conf
(LANE_MACHINE_CONF). Check-in stamps are ~/.cache/lane-control/night/<name>.

Exit: 0 something is due; 1 nothing is due (a coordinator whose idle time is unknown, or a runner list gh cannot
read, is named on stderr); 2 it cannot tell (no or a bad machine.conf, an unreadable session folder or store): the
run is skipped and stderr says why.
"""
import datetime as dt
import os
import sqlite3
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))
import harnesses  # noqa: E402
import improve  # noqa: E402
import machineconf  # noqa: E402


def stamp_dir() -> Path:
    v = os.environ.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME")
    base = Path(v) if v and os.path.isabs(v) else Path.home() / ".cache"
    return base / "lane-control" / "night"


def err(msg: str):
    print(f"night-precheck: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)


def checked(name: str, kind: str = "") -> int:
    if not machineconf.NAME.fullmatch(name or "") or kind not in ("", "improve", "wrapup"):
        err("--checked takes a coordinator name from machine.conf, and optionally `improve` or `wrapup`, "
            f"got {name!r}{' ' + kind if kind else ''}")
        return 2
    d = stamp_dir()
    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (d / (f"{name}.{kind}" if kind else name)).touch()
    if kind:
        try:
            (d / f"{name}.{kind}.pending").replace(d / f"{name}.{kind}.idle")
        except FileNotFoundError:
            (d / f"{name}.{kind}.idle").unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return 0


UNKNOWN_STAMP = ".budget-unknown"
UNKNOWN_QUIET_H = 16


def budget_gate(project: str = "") -> "tuple[str, str]":
    """('ok', ''), ('push', why) at no-new-work or push-and-handover (or the window at 95 or 98), ('stopped', why) at
    the stop step, or ('unknown', why)."""
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([str(here / "budget-state"), *(["--project", project] if project else [])], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return "unknown", f"budget-state failed ({e})"
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return "unknown", (r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ["budget-state failed"])[-1].removeprefix("budget-state: ")
    lines = r.stdout.splitlines()
    if not lines:
        return "unknown", "no metered budget in the config"
    for line in lines:
        f = line.split()
        if len(f) > 1 and f[1] == "unknown":
            return "unknown", line
    push = ""
    for line in lines:
        kv = dict(x.split("=", 1) for x in line.split()[1:] if "=" in x)
        step, wstep = kv.get("step", "0"), kv.get("window_step", "0")
        step = int(step) if step.isdigit() else 0
        if step >= 4:
            return "stopped", line
        if step >= 2 or (wstep.isdigit() and int(wstep) >= 1):
            push = push or line
    return ("push", push) if push else ("ok", "")


NUDGE_WAIT_CAP_MIN = 480
REPLY_GRACE_MIN = 10   # a session write this soon after a nudge is the coordinator's reply to it, not work


def nudge_state(name: str, kind: str, idle: float, now: float) -> "tuple[float, float | None]":
    """(idle, wait): how long the coordinator has effectively been idle, and how long to wait after the last nudge
    (None when there was none). The nudge is delivered into the session and asks for a one-line reply, so the session
    writes around it, before `--checked` stamps it or after: a write within REPLY_GRACE_MIN either side of the stamp is
    not work, and the idle time at the last nudge, kept in a sidecar file when the line went out, carries on from
    there. A write later than that is work: the wait starts over."""
    stamp = stamp_dir() / f"{name}.{kind}"
    try:
        age = (now - stamp.stat().st_mtime) / 60
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return idle, None
    wrote = age - idle   # minutes after the nudge the session last wrote (negative: before it)
    if wrote < -REPLY_GRACE_MIN or (wrote <= 0 and not (stamp_dir() / f"{name}.{kind}.idle").exists()):
        return idle, idle - age
    if wrote <= REPLY_GRACE_MIN:
        try:
            before = float((stamp_dir() / f"{name}.{kind}.idle").read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            before = 0.0
        return before + age, before
    return idle, 0.0


def nudge_due(name: str, kind: str, idle: float, min_idle: int, now: float) -> "tuple[bool, float]":
    """(due, idle): whether an improve or wrap-up nudge for `name` is due, and the idle time it counts. It has been idle
    `min_idle` minutes and the last nudge is at least that old; while it stays idle the wait grows to the idle time at
    the last nudge (30, 60, 120 minutes, at most 8 h), so a coordinator waiting on a long lane is not woken every half
    hour, and a reply to the nudge does not reset it."""
    eff, wait = nudge_state(name, kind, idle, now)
    if eff < min_idle:
        return False, eff
    if wait is None:
        return True, eff
    age = (now - (stamp_dir() / f"{name}.{kind}").stat().st_mtime) / 60
    return age >= min_idle and age >= min(max(min_idle, wait), NUDGE_WAIT_CAP_MIN), eff


def remember_nudges(lines: list, effective: dict):
    """Keep the idle time each emitted nudge counted; `--checked` makes it the last nudge's, for the next run's reply
    check (until then a repeated run computes from the same earlier value)."""
    for line in lines:
        f = line.split()
        if len(f) > 2 and f[0] == "DUE" and f[2] in ("improve", "wrapup") and (f[1], f[2]) in effective:
            d = stamp_dir()
            d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            (d / f"{f[1]}.{f[2]}.pending").write_text(str(int(effective[(f[1], f[2])])))


def wrapup_lines(wrap: list, drain: dict, now: float) -> list:
    """The `DUE <name> wrapup` lines: the mode has ended but these coordinators have not wrapped up (`lane-improve
    drained`). Not gated by the budget except at the stop step: a wrap-up is a push, a draft PR and a summary."""
    waited = int((now - dt.datetime.fromisoformat(drain["ended"]).timestamp()) / 3600)
    out = []
    for name, idle in wrap:
        gate, why = ("ok", "") if drain["unmetered"] else budget_gate(name)
        if gate == "stopped":
            err(f"{name}: budget at the stop step ({why}): no wrap-up nudge")
        else:
            out.append(f"DUE {name} wrapup idle={idle}min waited={max(waited, 0)}h")
    return out


def cap_wrapup_lines(capwrap: list, istate: dict) -> list:
    """The `DUE <name> wrapup ... cap=` lines: the project's cap is reached, so it wraps up (a push, a summary PR, a
    message). Gated only at the stop step, as an ended period's wrap-up is."""
    out = []
    for name, idle, hit in capwrap:
        gate, why = ("ok", "") if istate["unmetered"] else budget_gate(name)
        if gate == "stopped":
            err(f"{name}: budget at the stop step ({why}): no wrap-up nudge")
        else:
            out.append(f"DUE {name} wrapup idle={idle}min cap={hit}")
    return out


def improve_lines(nudge: list, istate: dict, now: float) -> list:
    """The `DUE <name> improve` lines for these (name, idle) pairs, after the budget: unmetered improve is not gated
    and never unknown; metered follows the project's own steps (no new cycle from no-new-work on, so no nudge)."""
    out = []
    for name, idle in nudge:
        line = f"DUE {name} improve idle={idle}min"
        if istate["unmetered"]:
            out.append(line)
            continue
        gate, why = budget_gate(name)
        if gate == "ok":
            out.append(line)
        elif gate == "unknown":
            stamp = stamp_dir() / UNKNOWN_STAMP
            try:
                said = now - stamp.stat().st_mtime < UNKNOWN_QUIET_H * 3600
            except FileNotFoundError:
                said = False
            if said:
                err(f"{name}: budget unknown ({why}): no improve nudge; already said so tonight")
            else:
                stamp.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                stamp.touch()
                out.insert(0, f"BUDGET unknown ({why}): no improve nudges until the usage feed gives a reading")
        elif gate == "push":
            # as for a plain check-in: it asks only to push and write the handover (no new cycle from here on)
            out.append(line)
            if not any(x.startswith("BUDGET push-and-handover") for x in out):
                out.insert(0, f"BUDGET push-and-handover ({why}): check-ins ask only to push and write the handover")
        else:
            err(f"{name}: budget at {gate} ({why}): no improve nudge")
    return out


def find(name: str) -> int:
    """`--find`: print `<harness> <handle> <title>` for the coordinator, or say on stderr why it cannot be found."""
    try:
        coords = [c for c in machineconf.coordinators(machineconf.load()) if c.name == name]
    except machineconf.ConfError as e:
        err(str(e))
        return 2
    if not coords:
        err(f"{name!r} is not a coordinator in {machineconf.path()}")
        return 2
    found, problems = machineconf.resolve(coords, handles=True)
    for why in problems:
        err(why)
    if not found:
        return 1
    w = found[0]
    print(f"{w.harness} {w.handle or '-'} {w.title}")
    return 0


def recently_checked(name: str, recheck_min: int, now: float) -> bool:
    try:
        return now - (stamp_dir() / name).stat().st_mtime < recheck_min * 60
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return False


def main(argv: list) -> int:
    if argv[:1] == ["--checked"] and len(argv) in (2, 3):
        return checked(*argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["--find"] and len(argv) == 2:
        return find(argv[1])
    if argv[:1] in (["-h"], ["--help"]):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 0
    if argv:
        err("usage: night-precheck [--checked <name> [improve|wrapup] | --find <name>]")
        return 2
    try:
        conf = machineconf.load()
        coords = machineconf.coordinators(conf)
        for c in coords:
            if c.harness:  # one given in machine.conf; the others are looked up from Orca, per project
                harnesses.load_harness(c.harness)
        away = machineconf.presence()
    except (machineconf.ConfError, ValueError) as e:
        err(str(e))
        return 2
    for w in conf["warnings"]:
        err(w)
    istate = improve.load()  # None = off; a file that cannot be used says why on stderr
    drain = None if istate else improve.draining()  # an ended period that has not been wrapped up
    owner_away = bool(away.get("LANE_OWNER_AWAY"))
    if not owner_away and not istate and not drain:  # improve mode's nudges do not wait for the owner to be away
        err(f"the owner is not away ({away.get('LANE_PRESENCE_WHY') or 'day'}): nothing is due")
        return 1
    now, due, broken = time.time(), [], False
    nudge = []  # coordinators improve mode covers that are due its resume check-in
    wrap = []   # coordinators of an ended period that are due a wrap-up nudge
    capwrap = []  # (name, idle, cap) of coordinators whose cap is reached and that are due a wrap-up nudge
    eff = {}    # (name, kind) -> the idle time a nudge counts (see nudge_state)
    if not coords:
        err(f"{machineconf.path()} lists no coordinators (is it still the unfilled example?): nobody to check in on")
    active = []
    for c in coords:
        try:
            if machineconf.paused(c.checkout):
                err(f"{c.name}: paused (project-pause), no check-in")
                continue
        except machineconf.ConfError as e:
            err(f"{c.name}: {e}; no check-in")
            continue
        active.append(c)
    located, problems = machineconf.resolve(active, titles=False)  # Orca is asked only for a line without its harness and title
    for why in problems:
        err(why)
    for c in located:
        try:
            idle = harnesses.load_harness(c.harness).idle_minutes(c.checkout, now, "coordinator")
        except (OSError, sqlite3.Error) as e:
            err(f"{c.name}: cannot read its {c.harness} session for {c.checkout} ({e}); skipping this run")
            broken = True
            continue
        if idle is None:
            err(f"{c.name}: no coordinator session recorded for {c.checkout}: it was not started with LANE_ROLE and "
                "LANE_PERSONA (project-setup starts it so), so its idle time is unknown and it gets no check-in")
            continue
        if istate and (istate["projects"] == "all" or c.name in istate["projects"]):
            # improve covers it: the resume nudge stands in for the plain check-in
            broken = improve.period_problem(istate)
            hit = None if broken or improve.is_wrapped(istate, c.name) else improve.caps(istate, c.name)[1]
            if broken:  # the caps fail closed: nothing can be known about wrap-ups, so nothing is nudged
                err(f"{c.name}: {broken}: no improve nudge (`lane-improve on --continue` starts the record again)")
            elif improve.is_wrapped(istate, c.name):
                err(f"{c.name}: wrapped up at its cap: no nudge")
            elif hit:  # a cap is reached: like the end time, for this project alone
                is_due, eff[(c.name, "wrapup")] = nudge_due(c.name, "wrapup", idle, conf["IMPROVE_IDLE_MIN"], now)
                if is_due:
                    capwrap.append((c.name, idle, hit))
            elif improve.rested(c.name):
                err(f"{c.name}: resting (nothing within the limits left): no improve nudge")
            else:
                is_due, eff[(c.name, "improve")] = nudge_due(c.name, "improve", idle, conf["IMPROVE_IDLE_MIN"], now)
                if is_due:
                    nudge.append((c.name, idle))
        elif drain and c.name in drain["pending"]:
            # the period ended: the wrap-up nudge stands in for the plain check-in
            is_due, eff[(c.name, "wrapup")] = nudge_due(c.name, "wrapup", idle, conf["IMPROVE_IDLE_MIN"], now)
            if is_due:
                wrap.append((c.name, idle))
        elif owner_away and idle >= conf["IDLE_MIN"] and not recently_checked(c.name, conf["RECHECK_MIN"], now):
            due.append(f"DUE {c.name} idle={idle}min")
    if due:  # coordinators due: the budget decides what, if anything, they get
        gate, why = budget_gate()
        if gate == "stopped":
            err(f"budget at the stop step ({why}): no check-ins")
            due = []
        elif gate == "push":
            due.insert(0, f"BUDGET push-and-handover ({why}): check-ins ask only to push and write the handover")
        elif gate == "unknown":
            stamp = stamp_dir() / UNKNOWN_STAMP
            try:
                said = now - stamp.stat().st_mtime < UNKNOWN_QUIET_H * 3600
            except FileNotFoundError:
                said = False
            if said:
                err(f"budget unknown ({why}): no check-ins; already said so tonight")
                due = []
            else:
                stamp.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                stamp.touch()
                due = [f"BUDGET unknown ({why}): no check-ins until the usage feed gives a reading"]
    elif coords and not broken and not nudge:
        gate, why = budget_gate()
        if gate == "unknown":
            err(f"budget unknown ({why}): no check-ins would go out (nobody is due now)")
    if nudge:
        due += improve_lines(nudge, istate, now)
    if wrap:
        due += wrapup_lines(wrap, drain, now)
    if capwrap:
        due += cap_wrapup_lines(capwrap, istate)
    for repo in machineconf.runner_repos(conf) if owner_away else []:  # improve's nudges by day do not bring runner lines
        try:
            off = machineconf.offline_runners(repo)
        except machineconf.RunnerError as e:
            err(f"runners of {e}: not counted")
            continue
        if off:
            due.append(f"OFFLINE {','.join(off)} repo={repo}")
    if broken:
        return 2
    remember_nudges(due, eff)
    for line in due:
        print(line)
    return 0 if due else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
